monotonic_clock
------------------------------------------
Provides access to a clock that always increases at the same rate. Unlike the
system time (e.g. gettimeofday()) this will never decrease. However, if there's
no monotonic clock on your system then this library will fall back to
gettimeofday().

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libmonotonic_clock-devel-0.01+git20191122-1bl1
  libmonotonic_clock0.01_0-0.01+git20191122-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/ThomasHabets/monotonic_clock

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/ThomasHabets/monotonic_clock.git

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack monotonic_clock-0.01+git20191122-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./monotonic_clock-0.01+git20191122-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/monotonic_clock-0.01+git20191122-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/monotonic_clock-0.01+git20191122-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libmonotonic_clock0.01_0-0.01+git20191122-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libmonotonic_clock-devel-0.01+git20191122-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

